# CANONICAL DRVI .gitattributes — copy this into every new repo at hydrate.
#
# Copy it as `.gitattributes` in the repo root, then run `git add --renormalize .` before the first
# commit. On a brand-new repo that command does nothing, which is the point: doing it at hydrate costs
# nothing and doing it later costs a whole-file rewrite of everything.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# Every text file marks the end of each line with an invisible character. Windows uses two of them;
# Linux and macOS use one. Git stores whatever was committed. So when a file stored the Linux way is
# edited on Windows, the editor rewrites EVERY line, and Git cannot tell "this line changed" from
# "this line's invisible ending changed". A two-line edit is then committed as a whole-file rewrite.
#
# That is not cosmetic. The real change is buried, review becomes impossible, merges conflict on lines
# nobody touched, and one person's work can be reverted without anyone seeing it happen.
#
# Recorded as PL-042 in `PAB-Memory:problem-log.md`. It was found four times in one session, once
# turning a two-line edit to `PAB-Memory:SOTU.md` into a 195-line diff that had to be reverted and
# redone by hand. On 2026-08-11 it was swept across every DRVI repository at once, which is exactly
# the work this template exists to stop anyone ever having to do again.
#
# WHAT `text=auto eol=lf` MEANS
# -----------------------------
# Store text as LF in the repository regardless of the machine that wrote it. Working copies are
# unaffected on every platform DRVI uses; only the stored blob is normalised. Verified on
# `safeshine-wtc` and again across 29 repositories: `git diff --ignore-all-space` reported zero
# non-whitespace differences every time.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and generated files — never touch these. Normalising a binary corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.grib2 binary
